CELL

You crawl through the hole in the wall and plop to the ground on the other
side. You find yourself in a dank, cramped cell far below Lot's castle. 
The room was originally used by the Romans for food storage, but someone 
converted it into a miserable dungeon by bolting chains to the clammy 
stone walls.

There is a cell door of stout wood to the north, and a hole in the wall to
the west where a stone has been pushed out. A prisoner is chained to the 
wall.

You see a building stone here.

