OUTSIDE CASTLE GATE

You walk outside the gate to the castle of evil King Lot. A soldier is 
standing guard. To the south is the village smithy.

The smith pulls you out of earshot of the guard and whispers, "I am 
grateful to you for freeing me, kind sir. I dare no longer stay in this 
town for fear of being recaptured by King Lot. But as thanks for freeing 
me, I will tell you where I have hidden another sword. It is plain, unlike
Lot's sword, but it is of the best quality. It is hidden under the roots 
of the oak tree in the village green. Goodbye, sir. And thank you again."

The smith walks off toward the town gate and quickly disappears from 
sight.

